WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:08.310
 

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.750
Happy Halloween, playas!

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:15.310
This week we gettin monstrous with
"Frankenstein," by Mary Shelley.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:23.140
When some playboy named Walton peeps some hood named Frankenstein in the North Pole,

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.940
they begin conversating, and 
Franky start spilling his life story.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:30.900
As a youngin, Victor Frankenstein
only got two things on his mind:

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.600
science, which he calls "natural philosophy,"

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.580
and his cousin Elizabeth's bangin booty. 
Mmh mmh mmh.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.240
In college, Victor gets so pro at the
science game that he gets drunk off da power

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.180
and decides it's time to try and create new life.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.420
The result of Victor's experiment is a
 busted-up monster so damn fugly

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.580
that Victor wigs out and trucks it straight outta town.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:58.340
Later, the monster rolls up on Victor while he's chillin and gives him the lowdown on what he's been up to.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:01.830
See, after escaping from Victor's stuffy-ass crib,

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:06.760
the monster posts up in some village, where he starts secretly creepin on one of the families.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:11.300
The monster learns all sorts of sh*t from these homies, like how to read and communicate,

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:17.220
but none of that fixes the fact he lonely as f**k. So he decide to go to try to chill with deez ballas.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:23.360
But as soon as they catch a glance at his janky-ass mug, they all tweak out and get the hell outta dodge.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:26.940
Then the monster say Victor gotta build him a nappy woman monster

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:31.260
that he gonna take to the wilds of South
America where they won't bother nobody.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.660
At first my boy Victor thinks it's a solid
idea, but then he starts thinking,

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:39.480
"Hold up! What if they start gettin freaky 
and make little monster babies?"

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.220
Ah hell naw!

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:46.640
Since Victor went back on his word, da monster gets all torn up and straight chokes a bitch —

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.280
Victor's bride Elizabeth.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:54.130
So Victor decide he gonna spend the rest of his days searchin the Earth to stomp that scrub.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:58.350
But it's a search Victor don't get to finish, 
cuz he dies chasin his creation.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:02.870
When da monster finds him layin in chalk,
he realizes that he's lonelier than eva,

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:04.890
and all that's left for him is death.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:14.320
Say dawg, listen up and let me school you on this book's subtitle — The Modern Prometheus —

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:19.680
which servin up some real talk on the similarities between Victor and the Titan Prometheus.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.900
In Greek myth, my homie Promie straight molded human beings outta some clay.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:29.420
And in certain stories, Prometheus was jonesin to give man a little taste of that heavenly fire.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:36.700
When he boosted it from the Gods, Zeus started trippin hard core. Just like that G'd up Titan, Victor jacks fire

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:42.040
from the sky that not only bringin a plague down on himself, but errybody in da hood.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:47.860
But why's everybody havin to ride this beef? Cuz Victor was chasin knowledge at the cost of errything else —

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.580
just like Adam when he claimin his
five finger discount from the Tree of Knowledge.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.260
And the biblical allusions don't stop there, son.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:03:00.680
As the original gangsta of the human race, Adam wakes up in Eden, is given a bangin hunny by his creator,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.960
and is ultimately kicked outta paradise.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:10.120
But Frankenstein's monster, as the first of its kind, wakes up in some broke-ass crib with body parts slung around,

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:15.620
watches his woman get ripped apart by his creator, and ain't neva gonna find no paradise.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.420
Sucks to be this fool.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:23.380
And it's exactly all this bunk-ass jive that leads the monster to act like Milton's Satan from "Paradise Lost,"

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:26.540
one of the only books the monster's ever read. Check it:

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:32.740
I had cast off all feeling, subdued all anguish, to riot in the excess of my despair.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:35.620
Evil henceforth became my good.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:42.400
So farewell Hope, and with Hope farewell Fear,
Farewell remorse: all Good to me is lost;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.720
Evil be thou my Good.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:51.340
But the monster ain't da only one slingin dem dark deeds. Nah, son. Victor sippin the same Koolaid.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:57.300
Not only do they both waste each other's bitty, but they handin out the same street justice — Vengeance.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:01.940
And when it's all said and done, Frankenstein and his monster ain't so different.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:06.360
All them blurry ethical lines point to the main thematic question up in here:

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.960
Are we inherently good or evil?

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.720
Are people driven to murder cuz of society's sh*t?

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:15.980
Or is it written from day one that a playa 
gonna be a cold-hearted killer?

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:20.720
And if so, who's to blame — the monster or the creator?

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:25.720
Yo, thanks for keepin it OG wit yo boy Sparky Sweets. Subscribe and tune in next week.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.240
Happy Halloween, b*tches.

